<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Lutician Federation</h1><p class="st-meta">983 CE – 1150 CE (approx.) · capital Rethra</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A pagan Slavic alliance east of the Elbe that destroyed German rule in 983 and was governed by assemblies and the oracle of the god at Rethra.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Lutici, or Veleti, were West Slavic tribes between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oder-river">Oder</a>, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redarii">Redarii</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tollensians">Tollensians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circipanians">Circipanians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kessinians">Kessinians</a>. In 983 they rose against German rule, destroying the bishoprics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havelberg">Havelberg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and expelling the margraves of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-march">Northern March</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-slav-rising">Great Slav Rising</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The federation had no prince; decisions were taken by assemblies of the tribes, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thietmar-of-merseburg">Thietmar of Merseburg</a> describes the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radegast">Radegast</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svarozic">Svarożic</a>) at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rethra">Rethra</a>, whose priests consulted oracles. Remarkably, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Henry II</a> allied with the pagan Lutici against the Christian Polish ruler Bolesław I, causing scandal among churchmen.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Internal war among the tribes in 1057 weakened the federation, and in 1068 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burchard-ii-of-halberstadt">Burchard of Halberstadt</a> destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rethra">Rethra</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wendish-crusade">Wendish Crusade</a> of 1147 and campaigns of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-pomerania">Duchy of Pomerania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-the-bear">Albert the Bear</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> absorbed the Lutician lands by the mid 12th century.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 983 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.26%;width:3.32%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>983 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rethra</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polabian (West Slavic)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Liutizi, Lutici, Veleti</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1066&amp;focus=lutician-federation" aria-label="Lutician Federation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4919 406 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lutician Federation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5239 662h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5239 662h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Germany. <a href="/a